<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saint-Jean-Pied-de-Port</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saint-Jean-Pied-de-Port is a small town in the French Basque Country, at the foot of the road over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a> to Roncesvalles. It was the chief town of Lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a>, the part of the Kingdom of Navarre north of the mountains, and is a major stop on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camino-frances">French Way</a> of the pilgrimage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago-de-compostela">Santiago de Compostela</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saint-jean-pied-de-port.jpg" alt="Saint-Jean-Pied-de-Port" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hayden Soloviev · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saint-Jean-Pied-de-Port.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
